yaml/string/literal-block
description: A | block — line breaks kept verbatim
- >
  A literal block starts with `|` and holds the following indented lines VERBATIM — every line
  break kept. Two qualifiers ride the header: CHOMPING — clip (the default), strip (`|-`),
  keep (`|+`) — and the INDENTATION INDICATOR (`|2`), pinning the content indent where the
  first line leaves it ambiguous:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  script: |
    line one
    line two
